<VI _name="lvai_typedef_tree.vi" description="List the controls of one container on a VI's or .ctl's front panel\2C with the typedef information the caller needs to walk the tree\3A each child's label\2C whether it is a typedef instance\2C the .ctl it points at\2C and its VI Server class name so the caller knows what can be descended into.\0A\0AWHY THE DESCENT IS BY INDEX AND NOT BY LABEL. Addressing a nested control by label needs a label lookup per level\2C which is a loop inside the descent loop - and AIXML auto-indexes a tunnel carrying a refnum array into an inner loop\2C which is one of the failure modes docs/aixml-reference.md records. By index the descent is a single flat loop. The caller already holds the indices\2C because it got them from the previous call to this same VI. An ARRAY element has no label of its own\2C which is a second reason label addressing could not have worked.\0A\0AIT DESCENDS INTO BOTH CLUSTERS AND ARRAYS\2C and they need different properties. Controls[] is declared on {LV.Cluster}\2C {LV.Panel}\2C {LV.ConnectorPane}\2C {LV.RadioButtonsControl} and {LV.WaveformData} - NOT on {LV.Array}\2C whose single child is reached through Array Element and comes back as ONE reference rather than an array. Both are read unconditionally and Select picks between them on Class Name\2C which keeps the descent one flat loop\3A a Case structure here would have to carry the refnum array through a tunnel\2C which is the auto-indexing trap above. The cast that does not apply fails harmlessly\2C its error deliberately unwired.\0A\0Aindex path is pipe separated because a newline cannot be used\3A the runner pairs its own control names and values by line. An EMPTY index path lists the panel's own controls\2C which is where a walk starts. An array contributes one segment like any other container and its only child is index 0.\0A\0AEVERY CHILD REPORTS ITS OWN READ CODE\2C and that is not tidiness. The loop chains one error per iteration and only the LAST one could ever reach the output\2C so a control whose property read failed came back as a plausible row - empty label\2C empty Typedef Path\2C empty Class Name - while the VI itself answered code 0. A caller keying on the empty path then skipped it in SILENCE. Measured 2026-09-18. Read `read codes` per element\3B a non-zero entry means that row is not to be trusted\2C and is NOT the same thing as a control that simply is not a typedef.\0A\0AREAD ONLY. Nothing here writes\2C so it is safe on a file that is also open elsewhere.">
